Private HFX 0.4.0 MERIT Hydro + MERIT Basins dataset.

Sources:
- MERIT Hydro v1.0.1 (Yamazaki et al., 2019), dual-licensed CC BY-NC 4.0 / ODbL 1.0; used under CC BY-NC 4.0 (NonCommercial). Original-format complete redistribution requires explicit permission.
- MERIT-Basins v0.7/v1.0_bugfix1 and Coastal Hillslopes (Lin et al., 2019), distributed via reachhydro.org under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and UCSD non-commercial/research license terms.

Transformations: native raster grids and direction codes preserved with ocean code 247 explicitly tagged as GeoTIFF nodata, river mouth code 0 and inland depression code 255 retained distinct under flow_dir_encoding='merit'. Vectors keep original coordinates, part order, and native attributes; invalid source polygons and degenerate zero-length self-referencing river records (NextDownID=up1=COMID, maxup=0) are omitted with explicit provenance rather than repaired. Upstream IDs in river-graph.parquet derive from verified incoming NextDownID links so confluences exceeding the shapefile's four up1..up4 slots retain all incoming edges while native maxup and up1..up4 columns stay intact. Eastern Chukotka vectors (pfaf_35 and hillslope_35) preserve native unwrapped antimeridian longitudes (>180 deg E, up to ~191.003 deg E) without clipping or splitting, while MERIT Hydro rasters span wrapped longitudes (~-180.0004 to +179.9996 deg), requiring -360 deg longitude wrapping and split antimeridian raster reads. Derived geodesic area_km2 uses the WGS84 ellipsoid and is distinct from native unitarea and uparea. Catchment connectivity is not_supplied; outlets, nodes, and upstream polygon area are null/absent.
